          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "To automate order processing, shop-floor data collection, and operations while keeping your core ERP intact, you need a partner skilled in **ERP “wrapper” architectures**—using Microsoft Power Platform (Power Apps, Power Automate, AI Builder) and Azure integration gateways to interface with existing on-premise or cloud databases.\n\nConsultants to evaluate include local Tasmanian partners (advantageous for assessing shop-floor physical workflows) as well as national specialists who bring pre-built manufacturing templates.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Local Tasmanian & Hobart-Based Consultants\n\nHaving a consultant who can physically walk your shop floor to inspect machine layout, Wi-Fi blind spots, operator ergonomics, and barcode scanning workflows is a major advantage.\n\n*   **ISW (Information Services Way)** *(Hobart HQ)*  \n    *   **Why them:** Founded and headquartered in Hobart, ISW has over 25 years of systems integration and software engineering experience. They specialize in connecting modern platforms like Microsoft 365 and Power Platform back into legacy business systems, on-premise databases, and third-party ERPs.\n    *   **Fit:** Ideal if your ERP lacks standard modern APIs and requires custom middleware, integration gateways, or hybrid data pipelines.\n*   **Intuit Technologies** *(Hobart / Launceston)*  \n    *   **Why them:** One of Tasmania’s largest ICT and Microsoft partners. They have an established Microsoft Cloud & Business Solutions practice with local Power Platform developers and solution architects.\n    *   **Fit:** Excellent for mid-to-large operational rollouts where you need both platform development and robust underlying IT/infrastructure support (e.g., networking the shop floor, mobile device management for warehouse tablets).\n*   **FutureAbility** *(Hobart-based)*  \n    *   **Why them:** A Hobart boutique dedicated specifically to Microsoft Power Platform and Copilot Studio automation for mid-market businesses. \n    *   **Fit:** Suited for agile, rapid-turnaround implementations (e.g., deploying focused Power Apps for order approvals or shop-floor defect logging) without the enterprise overhead of a large MSP.\n*   **Dialog Information Technology (NCS Group)** *(Hobart Office)*  \n    *   **Why them:** Maintains a longstanding delivery presence in Hobart and has deep expertise across Microsoft enterprise applications, custom application development, and industrial data integrations.\n\n---\n\n### 2. National Australian Manufacturing Specialists (Hybrid Delivery)\n\nThese firms frequently service Tasmanian manufacturing remotely, supported by fly-in/fly-out site visits for scoping and go-live:\n\n*   **Barhead Solutions** *(Melbourne / Sydney)*  \n    *   **Why them:** Recognized as one of Australia’s leading Microsoft Business Applications and Power Platform partners. They have significant experience designing \"wrapper\" front-ends over legacy core systems specifically for field operations, warehousing, and production line data collection.\n*   **Professional Advantage** *(Melbourne / National)*  \n    *   **Why them:** Longstanding specialists in mid-market Australian manufacturing and distribution operations. Because they implement both ERPs and integration layers, their team understands how to read/write production orders, BOMs, and work center routing without corrupting ERP transactional logic.\n*   **Rapid Circle** *(National with Tasmanian footprint / TasICT member)*  \n    *   **Why them:** Tier-1 Microsoft Cloud and Power Platform partner. Strong background in workflow governance, Centre of Excellence (CoE) setup, and automating manual processes across industrial and operational environments.\n\n---\n\n### What to Ask Them During Scoping\n\nTo ensure the prospective partner understands the nuances of manufacturing automation around a legacy ERP, press them on the following:\n\n1.  **ERP Integration Architecture:**  \n    *   *Question:* *\"How will Power Platform connect to our specific ERP?\"*  \n    *   *Look for:* Experience using the **Microsoft On-Premises Data Gateway**, Azure Logic Apps, REST/OData connectors, or direct SQL read-only replicas. They should emphasize protecting ERP data integrity (e.g., staging tables or validation APIs rather than unsafe direct database writes).\n2.  **Order Processing Automation:**  \n    *   *Question:* *\"How do you handle incoming orders from email/PDF without manual re-keying?\"*  \n    *   *Look for:* Use of **Power Automate + AI Builder Document Processing** to extract data from customer purchase orders, run automated reconciliation against your ERP master pricing and SKU tables, and only route exceptions to humans for approval.\n3.  **Shop-Floor Environmental Realities:**  \n    *   *Question:* *\"How will the shop-floor app handle offline states and industrial peripherals?\"*  \n    *   *Look for:* Knowledge of Power Apps offline canvas caching, hardware barcode scanner integration (via camera or dedicated Zebra/Honeywell Android scanners), and large-touch interface design for operators wearing PPE/gloves.\n4.  **Licensing Strategy:**  \n    *   *Question:* *\"How do we license 30+ shop-floor operators cost-effectively?\"*  \n    *   *Look for:* Pragmatic advice on Microsoft licensing. Naming every shift worker with an individual Power Apps Premium license can become expensive; a good consultant will advise on **Power Apps per-app licensing**, shared device configurations, or hybrid Power Pages/Power Automate alternatives.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
          ],
